100: /**
101:  * A serialized representation of decisions made during a query's execution.
102:  *
103:  * A journal is produced when a query function first executes and is re-used
104:  * when a query is re-executed.
105:  *
106:  * Currently this is used to store pagination end cursors to ensure
107:  * that pages of paginated queries will always end at the same cursor. This
108:  * enables gapless, reactive pagination.
109:  *
110:  * `null` is used to represent empty journals.
111:  * @public
112:  */
